      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Integrating Automated Agents Into Single-Engine Cockpit Operations: A Developmental Study\"\n",
        "author: \"Brock Rouser\"\n",
        "filters:\n",
        "   - include-code-files\n",
        "format: \n",
        "    revealjs:\n",
        "        #chalkboard: \n",
        "        #    buttons: true\n",
        "        self-contained: true\n",
        "        incremental: false\n",
        "        slide-number: true\n",
        "        theme: custom.scss\n",
        "        logo: https://ceat.okstate.edu/marketing-and-communications/site_files/imgs/osu-primary-logo.png\n",
        "        transition: 'fade'\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# Background\n",
        "## Summary Of Aircraft Evaluations \n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {layout=\"[ 0.55, -0.05, 0.4 ]\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n",
        "\\\n",
        "Aircraft design and development in commercial and military sectors has progressed at a rapid pace from powered flight in 1903 to modern automated and unmanned systems.\n",
        "Design evaluation in aviation is multidisciplinary including individual subsystem design evaluations. Traditionally subsystems can be evaluated in isolation easily such as in wind tunnel testing and CFD simulations. \n",
        "\n",
        "\\\n",
        "However, overall aircraft characteristics which stem from the combination\n",
        "of various subsystems is evaluated using test pilot feedback which is often limited due to sample size. Additionally, pilot feedback is usually captured via subjective\n",
        "self assessment which can be prone to bias and may not capture intricacies between individual aircraft subsystems.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
        "![*Brief History*](media/timeline.png)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: \n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## leveraging Sensors In Evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "Existing literature suggests a link between various physiological signals and operator states such as workload and situational awareness.\n",
        "With increasing accessability of sensor hardware and compute resources, studies suggest using time-series physiological sensors to quantify such\n",
        "operator states using sensors such as:\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.incremental}\n",
        "- Eye Trackers\n",
        "- Heart Rate Monitors (HRM)\n",
        "- Electroencephalogram (EEG)\n",
        "- Functional Near-Infrared Spectroscopy (fNIRS)\n",
        "- Galvanic Skin Response\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-up}\n",
        "Such sensing modalities may allow for new aircraft design considerations and may be useful in evaluating new aircraft as physiological signals\n",
        "can provide a layer of objective data alongside self assessment techniques.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Capability Development \n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {layout=\"[ 0.55, -0.05, 0.4 ]\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n",
        "The rise in popularity of complicated autonomous systems has shifted focus onto the pilot in aviation safety. \n",
        "The interplay between automation, mental workload, and situational awareness has become a topic of scrutiny as literature suggests that increased automation can result in an overall decrease in operator performance.\n",
        "\n",
        "\\\n",
        "With readily available sensors and advanced modeling techniques, some researchers have proposed frameworks to increase pilot awareness by adapting the amount of automation in the cockpit by using various time series data channels to quantify cognative states.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-left}\n",
        "![Taheri Gorji, H., Wilson, N., VanBree, J. et al](https://media.springernature.com/full/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41598-023-29647-0/MediaObjects/41598_2023_29647_Fig3_HTML.png?as=webp)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-left}\n",
        "![Yiu,C., Y., Ng, K., K., H., Li, Q., and Yuan, X.](media/models3_2.png)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: \n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Data Acquisition\n",
        "## Data Acquisition Challenges\n",
        "Utilizing a variety of physiological sensing modalities has several practical challenges that must be overcome to facilitate analysis for time-series data.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-left}\n",
        "- Software Dependencies\n",
        "    - Various sensor libraries provided by vendors require different operating systems, programming languages, and processor architecture (32 vs 64 bit)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-left}\n",
        "- Storage\n",
        "    - High frequency data from various sources should be stored in a common database in a common format\n",
        "    - Due to time-series nature of the data, synchronization is paramount to a high quality analysis\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-left}\n",
        "- Scalability\n",
        "    - Physiological data collection in an ecological setting may require different sensors for different tasks and may even need to consider multiple operators\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Development History\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {layout=\"[ 0.5, 0.1, 0.4 ]\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: column\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-left}\n",
        "<div style=\"border: 2px solid #ccc; padding: 10px; border-radius: 8px; margin-right: 10px;\">\n",
        "\n",
        "Initial LabVIEW Prototyping\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {layout=\"[50,50]\"}\n",
        "::: column\n",
        "<img src=\"media/labview/EEG.png\" style=\"width:90%; height:auto;\" />\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: column\n",
        "<img src=\"media/labview/cogstates.png\" style=\"height:100%; width:auto;\" />\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {layout=\"[50,50]\"}\n",
        "::: column\n",
        "<img src=\"media/labview/hmap.png\" style=\"width:100%; height:auto;\" />\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: column\n",
        "<img src=\"media/labview/eyetracking.png\" style=\"width:100%; height:auto;\" />\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "</div>\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: column\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-left}\n",
        "<div style=\"border: 2px solid #ccc; padding: 10px; border-radius: 8px;\">\n",
        "Intermediate Version\n",
        "\n",
        "::: column\n",
        "<img src=\"media/intermediateVersion/cogstates.png\" style=\"width:100%; height:auto;\" />\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: column\n",
        "<img src=\"media/intermediateVersion/rawEEG.png\" style=\"width:100%; height:auto;\" />\n",
        ":::\n",
        "</div>\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Current Software Architecture\n",
        "\n",
        "To overcome these challenges, a novel data acquisition system was developed utilizing open source tools and a distributed architecture.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column}\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"1\"}\n",
        "- Top layer uses a single control application to take in user input for testing configuration (which sensors, participant id#, etc.)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"2\"}\n",
        "- Listeners receive configuration and manage sensor processes\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"3\"}\n",
        "- Sensors utilize MQTT Broker to route data to appropriate subscribers\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"4\"}\n",
        "- Subscribers include:\n",
        "    - Common time-series database (InfluxDB)\n",
        "    - Web based visualizations for real time dashboards (Grafana)\n",
        "    - Real time processing applications (Statistical models)\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column .fragment data-fragment-index=\"0\"}\n",
        "![*Current Architecture*](media/architecture.png)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Operational Realism Test Framework\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.r-stack}\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "<img src=\"media/ortfControl.png\" width=\"900\" height=\"600\">\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "<img src=\"media/flightsimCCTV.png\" width=\"900\" height=\"600\">\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "<img src=\"media/grafana.png\" width=\"900\" height=\"600\">\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Experimental Work\n",
        "## Workload and Automation\n",
        "\n",
        "First battery of tests were focused on evaluating sensor capabilities and inferential modeling of multivariate physiological datasets. Experimental procedures focused on two independent variables.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column}\n",
        "- Working memory load via secondary task (n-back)\n",
        "- Automation state (autopilot on/off)\n",
        "\n",
        "Data acquired included EEG, HRM, NASA-TLX, and flight metrics. The total dataset exported from the common time-series database contained ~145 million records.\n",
        "\n",
        "Initial frequentist analysis failed when modeling physiological data due to invalid assumptions of independence and linearity. Due to this, analysis utilized general multivariate mixed effects modeling with parameters optimized via Bayesian MCMC sampling.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column}\n",
        "![*Experimental Flight Path*](media/acoko_path.png)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Linear Modeling\n",
        "Univariate and multivariate linear models can be optimized via ordinary least squares fitting \n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Y= \\beta X + \\epsilon\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\beta = (X^TX)^{-1}X^Ty\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "However, this requires several assumptions which are dependant on data:\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.incremental}\n",
        "- Normality in residuals\n",
        "- Linear parameters\n",
        "- No multicolinearity\n",
        "- homoscedasticity (constant residual variance )\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "Violating these assumptions will result in a model that doesn't fit well\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Bayesian Solution\n",
        "\n",
        "Bayes' theorem is expressed as:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(A|B)=\\frac{P(B|A) \\cdot P(A)}{P(B)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment}\n",
        "Considering our model parameters as a distribution allows for estimation via application of this theorem.\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(\\beta | y,X)=\\frac{P(y| \\beta, X) \\cdot P(\\beta | X)}{P(y | X)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns }\n",
        "::: {.column .fragment}"
      ],
      "id": "b614d11d"
    },
