      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Results\n",
        "\n",
        "![*TLX Ranges*](media/tlxScores.png){width=40%}\n",
        "\n",
        "![*Mean Parameters From Distributions*](media/table.png){width=50%}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Spatial Disorientation\n",
        "\n",
        "Continuing experimentation focused on the concept of spatial disorientation (SD) in aviation. This study investigated the physiological and cognitive effects of an induced SD illusion during simulated flight using multimodal sensor data. \n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"30%\"}\n",
        "- Visual and vestibular illusions administered via motion decoupling\n",
        "- Data acquired included EEG, HRM, NASA-TLX, and flight metrics\n",
        "\n",
        "A similar analysis approach was utilized after frequentist modeling checks failed. Additionally, this study focused on exploring different priors for model parameters \n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"65%\"}\n",
        "![*Fight Simulator*](media/SD/Figure1.png)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Model Checks\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"30%\"}\n",
        "\\\n",
        "\n",
        "A limitation of Bayesian General Linear Modeling is the potential bias introduced when using improper priors. All channels passed statistical tests for univariate normality, but failed for multivariate normality.\n",
        "\n",
        "Two families of distributions were used as priors for HR/RR and posterior predictive checks were conducted to evaluate model fit.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"70%\"}\n",
        "![](media/SD/Figure3.png){.absolute top=\"200\" left=\"400\" width=\"60%\" height=\"auto\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Model Comparison\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"30%\"}\n",
        "\\\n",
        "\n",
        "Subsets of EEG/Lifemonitor response variables compared to combined set and use of residual correlation estimated evaluated\n",
        "\n",
        "- ELPD difference indicates how closely two models differ in their posterior predictions \n",
        "- Best model indicated by 0 ELPD difference\n",
        "- SE difference indicates the difference in standard error between two models\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"70%\"}\n",
        "![](media/SD/comparison.png){.absolute top=\"200\" left=\"400\" width=\"60%\" height=\"auto\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Final Model Parameters {}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
        "\\\n",
        "\n",
        "Final model utilized Gaussian priors to allow for estimation of residual covariance. Values of parameters indicate the normalized change in the response variable during SD illusions.\n",
        "\n",
        "- Horizontal lines indicates mean and 1st quantile for each channel \n",
        "- X-axis width for each channel indicates likelihood of the parameter value\n",
        "- Captures variance and uncertainty in physiological channels changing with periods of SD illusions\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column}\n",
        "![](media/SD/Figure4.png){.absolute top=\"200\" left=\"500\" width=\"50%\" height=\"auto\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Physiological Correlates of Cognitive States\n",
        "\\\n",
        "\n",
        "The developed capability to collect and analyze physiological data in ecological environments poses many challenges when considering real-time applications. The two experiments conducted showcase the confounding nature of EEG responses across cognitive states such as mental workload, engagement, and spatial/situational awareness. The modeling displayed in these results highlights how the complicated nature of physiological datasets lends itself to equally complex modeling techniques. Complex algorithms have become more ubiquitous and may be able to lend predictability over readability. Such models include:\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {columns}\n",
        ":::{.column width=\"33%\" .fragment .fade-up}\n",
        "<img src=\"media/svm.png\" width=\"auto\" height=\"200\">\n",
        "<figcaption>*Mammone, A., Turchi, M., and Cristianini, N*</figcaption>\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.column width=\"33%\" .fragment .fade-up}\n",
        "<img src=\"media/1_CNN-1.png\" width=\"auto\" height=\"200\">\n",
        "<figcaption>*Qin, Z.,Yu F.,Liu, C., and Chen, X.*</figcaption>\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.column width=\"33%\" .fragment .fade-up}\n",
        "<img src=\"media/transformer.png\" width=\"auto\" height=\"200\">\n",
        "<figcaption>*Khan, S., Naseer, M., Hayat, M., et. al.*</figcaption>\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Adaptive Automation\n",
        "## What is adaptive vs adaptable automation\n",
        "\n",
        "::::{.columns}\n",
        ":::{.column}\n",
        "The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration has formalized levels of autonomy in vehicles. In the most extreme examples of autonomous systems such as full self driving cars the level of autonomy is decided by the driver. This is an example of adaptable automation.\n",
        "\n",
        "Adaptive automation refers to autonomous systems in which the system itself adjusts its level of autonomy in response to certain conditions. An example of this is auto ground collision avoidance system in the F-35.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.column}\n",
        "![*Anderson E, Fannin T, Nelson B.*](media/autonomy.png){width=80%}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Want to talk about agentic vs advisory system and levels of autonomy\n",
        "\n",
        "Due to the rise of agentic AI capable of taking in information, planning, and executing tasks, it may not be long until such systems are implemented in the aviation sector. \n",
        "\n",
        "The use of physiological data may benefit the development of such systems. Leveraging ecologically valid data may both benefit developers as an additional real-time stream of pilot state as well as evaluators who need to be able to assess whether an autonomous system is actually helpful from a human factors perspective.\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n",
        "  <img src=\"media/preliminary-time-series.png\" height=\"360\">\n",
        "  <figcaption>*Preliminary Workload Model*</figcaption>\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Preliminary Results\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column}\n",
        "\n",
        "- Existing work showed statistical significance of processed time-series data\n",
        "    - Power Spectral Densities\n",
        "    - Heart/Respiratory Rate\n",
        "    - Heart Rate Variability\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment  data-fragment-index=\"1\"}\n",
        "- By letting a deep learning model analyze the raw data, it can infer these processed features naturally and draw significance\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment  data-fragment-index=\"2\"}\n",
        "- A flaw in previous DAQ version caused significant data loss for preliminary model\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment  data-fragment-index=\"3\"}\n",
        "- New EEG data is currently being collected. A cleaning pipeline using independent component analysis is currently under construction\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column}\n",
        ":::: {.r-stack}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-out data-fragment-index=\"2\"}\n",
        "<img src=\"media/nova_1.2_resnet18.png\" width=\"250\">\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment  data-fragment-index=\"2\"}\n",
        "<img src=\"media/rawEEG.png\" width=\"450\">\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"3\"}\n",
        "<img src=\"media/cleanEEG.png\" width=\"450\">\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Plan and Proposal\n",
        "\n",
        ":::::{.column}\n",
        "::::: {.r-stack }\n",
        "::::{.fragment .fade-out data-fragment-index=\"3\" }\n",
        "The overarching gaps in literature this contribution seeks to fill are the following\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"0\"}\n",
        "- What are the practical limitations to implementing adaptive automation in aviation?\n",
        "    - Display design\n",
        "    - Trust in automation\n",
        "    - Tradeoffs between workload an automation\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"1\"}\n",
        "- Is adaptive automation better than adaptable?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"2\"}\n",
        "- Should the level of autonomy be constrained? And if so, by how much?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::::{.fragment .fade-in data-fragment-index=\"3\"}\n",
        "The proposed methodology for this work includes the following\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"6\" .highlight-red}\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"4\"}\n",
        "- Collection of contextual and physiological data in a variety of environments\n",
        "    - Flight simulators\n",
        "    - Multi-Attribute Task Battery (MATB)\n",
        "    - Other virtual environments\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"7\" .highlight-red}\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"5\"}\n",
        "- Development and usage of deep learning models trained on physiological data\n",
        "    - Bayesian optimization\n",
        "    - Multiclass outputs\n",
        "    - Hybrid models\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        ":::::\n",
        ":::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::::{.column}\n",
        "::::: {.r-stack }\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"6\"}\n",
        "Project Risks\n",
        "\n",
        "\\\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"6\"}\n",
        "- Data Collection\n",
        "    - IRB Logistics\n",
        "    - Sample size\n",
        "    - Normalization\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment data-fragment-index=\"7\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\\ \n",
        "\n",
        "- Training And Development\n",
        "    - Memory/compute power\n",
        "    - Vanishing/exploding gradients\n",
        "    - Overfitting \n",
        "    - Prediction speed for real-time application\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
